Subject: [PATCH] fix: keep the slice margins of a sliced MaskTexture

A MaskTexture with SetTextureSliceMargins was stretched whole across its
rect: a small rounded-corner mask (EllesmereUI's tooltips, borders and
bars) blurred the full rect instead of rounding its corners. Masked
quads are now split at the mask's slice lines, so its margins keep
their texel size and only its centre stretches, as for a sliced
texture. The split quads' texture requests and the mask request cover
the new vertices. A mask without room for its margins stretches whole.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
